---
import StudioLayout from '../../layouts/StudioLayout.astro';
---
<StudioLayout title="Kinetic Theory of Gases - Physics with Harshith" chapterChip="Physics · Kinetic Theory">

  <!-- =========== HOME =========== -->
  <section id="home" class="screen active">
    <div class="hero">
      <h1>Kinetic Theory <span class="accent">of Gases</span></h1>
      <p>A gas is just a huge number of tiny molecules flying around and bouncing off the walls. Every one of those bounces pushes on the wall - add them all up and you get pressure. Follow that one idea all the way to temperature and molecular speed.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">

      <div class="tile" onclick="location.href='/kinetic-theory/pressure-of-an-ideal-gas'">
        <div class="tile-num">01</div>
        <div class="tile-icon ic-gas"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><circle cx="8" cy="9" r="1.5"/><circle cx="15" cy="7" r="1.5"/><circle cx="11" cy="15" r="1.5"/><path d="M16.5 13.5l3 1.5M9.5 9.5l2-1"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Pressure of an Ideal Gas</h3>
        <p>Slides. One molecule in a cube, one collision, then all N of them - pressure from momentum, then kinetic energy, temperature, v<sub>rms</sub> and the Maxwell-Boltzmann speed distribution.</p>
        <span class="tile-go">Open slides &rsaquo;</span>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

</StudioLayout>

<style>
  .ic-gas { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0e7490, #22d3ee); }
</style>
